Now we proceed with the lemma. Let the radii of  $\omega_1$  and  $\omega_2$  be  $r_1, r_2$  respectively. By the previous lemma, we have   $$ \frac{(2 \cdot 15 + r_1r_2)(2r_1+15r_2)(2r_2+15r_1)}{(16-2)(16-15)(16-r_1)(16-r_2)} = (4R)^2 = \frac{(15 \cdot 16+r_1r_2)(15r_1+16r_2)(15r_2+16r_1)}{(23-15)(23-16)(23-r_1)(23-r_2)}. $$   Simplifying this,  $$ \frac{(30+r_1r_2)(30r_1^2+30r_2^2+229r_1r_2)}{(256-16r_1-16r_2+r_1r_2) \cdot 14 \cdot 1} = \frac{(240+r_1r_2)(240r_1^2+240r_2^2+481r_1r_2)}{8 \cdot 7 \cdot (529-23r_1-23r_2+r_1r_2)}. $$   Now let  $x = r_1r_2$ , and observe that  $r_1+r_2 = 15$ . We obtain
