Let  $p_n$  be the probability for a circle with numbers  $1, 2, \dots, n$ . Because the condition is true for  $n$  all of the time, we are inspired to write a recursion based on how  $n$  is inserted into the  $n-1$  case. Due to the condition, then  $n$  and  $n-1$  must have a distance of at most  $2$ .
-------------------
