Then treating the  $n$  and  $n-1$  like just  $n-1$ , we are in the  $n-1$  case. Thus the probability here is  $\frac{2}{n-1}\cdot p_{n-1}$ .
-------------------
<span style="color:blue">**Case 2: the distance is 2.**</span> Again, there is a  $\frac{2}{n-1}$  probability of this case.
[asy]
