<blockquote>Let  $I$  be the circumcenter of cyclic quadrilateral  $WXYZ$ , and let  $A,B,C,D$  be the midpoints of  $XY,YZ,ZW,WX$  respectively. Let  $O_1,O_2$  be the reflections of  $I$  in lines  $AD$  and  $CD$ , and let  $O_3$  be the reflection of  $I$  in line  $O_1O_2$ . Prove that  $B,I,O_3$  are collinear.</blockquote>

Let  $E,F$  be the feet of  $I$  onto  $AD$  and  $CD$ . Clearly it is equivalent to prove that line  $EF$  is parallel to line  $XY$  (since  $IB \perp XY$  and  $IO_3 \perp O_1O_2 \parallel EF$ ). 
