By using the same idea, we have  $\sum\limits_{i=1}^{b} h(u_k,u_i)=h_{B,k}$  and  $\sum\limits_{j=1}^{w} h(v_k,v_j)=h_{W,k}$ .

Now consider   $$ \sum\limits_{i=1}^{b}\sum\limits_{j=1}^{w}  h(u_i,v_j) = \sum\limits_{i=1}^{b}\left(H-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{b} h(u_i,u_j)\right)=bH-\sum\limits_{i=1}^{b} h_{B,i}=bH-2\cdot\text{area}(B) $$  Similarly, we have  $bH-2\cdot\text{area}(B)=wH-2\cdot\text{area}(W)$ . Thus, difference between area of  $B$  and  $W$  is  $\frac{b-w}{2}H$  which is independent to the way of coloring as desired.  
