Meaning that our answer is  $3 \cdot 8 = \boxed{24}$

By matching terms with its conjugate, we get that 
\begin{align*}
  (1 + \omega^k + \omega^{3k})(1 + \omega^{7 - k} + \omega^{3(7 - k)}) & = 1 + \omega^{- k} + \omega^{- 3k} 
  & \quad + \omega^k + 1 + \omega^{-2k} 
  & \quad \quad + \omega^{3k} + \omega^{2k} + 1 
  & = 3 + (-1) = 2
\end{align*}
Thus, the answer is  $2^3 \cdot 3 = \boxed{24}.$

