\[\angle APQ = 180^\circ - (\angle QPB + \angle BPC) = 180^\circ - (\theta + 3\theta) = 180^\circ - 4\theta\]
And,
\[\angle PRC = 180^\circ - \angle PRB = 2(\angle RBP) = 180^\circ - 4\theta. \]
This gives  $\angle APQ = \angle PRC$ . It also implies  $\angle AO_1Q = \angle PO_2C$  and we are done proving the claim.  $\square$  
----------
From the parallelogram, we get
    \[\overline{O_1O_2} = \overline{RQ} = \overline{BR}\]
and the solution is complete.  $\blacksquare$

