 $m+12n=889 \implies n \leq 74$ , so trying  $n=73$ , we get  $m=13$ ,  $p=163$ .
Now, we take mod  $13$ .
Then, 
\begin{align*}
    2m-n &\equiv 5 \pmod{13} 
    3m-2n &\equiv 10 \pmod{13} 
    \therefore 4m-2n &\equiv 10 \pmod{13} \implies 13 \mid m
\end{align*}
Thus, since  $m$  is prime,  $m=13 \implies n=73 \implies p=163$

