If we have  $a=b$  then we get  $pb = pc$  which implies that  $a=b=c$ . Hence we can safely assume that  $a,b$  are distinct. Thus,  $a^n-b^n$  and cyclic multiplication gives us \[(a^n - b^n)(b^n-c^n)(c^n - a^n) = \prod_{\text{cyc}} \left(\frac{a^n-b^n}{a-b}\right) = -p^3\] Since we know that  $\frac{a^n-b^n}{a-b} \in \mathbb{Z}$  , therefore we get  
\begin{align*} 
\frac{a^n-b^n}{a-b} &= \frac{p(c-b)}{a-b}  
&= p_c \in \{\pm 1 , \pm p , \pm p^2 , \pm p^3 \} 
\end{align*} define  $p_a$  and  $p_b$  similarly and  $p_ap_bp_c = -p^3$ However the system 
\begin{align*} 
p(c-b) &= p_c(a-b)  
p(b-a) &= p_b(c-a)  
p(a-c) &= p_a(b-c)
\end{align*}  
is true if and only if \[(b-c)(p_1p-p^2-p_1p_2) = 0\] Since we know that  
\begin{align*} 
p_1p-p^2-p_1p_2 &= 0  
\iff p_1(p-p_2) &= p^2  
\implies p - p_2 &\mid p^2  
\implies p &= 2
\end{align*}  
Hence if  $p \ge 3$  , it implies that  $b=c$  and we are done. 
